Subject: [PATCH] fritchii-reloc-guard-addr on fritchii-relocate-v2.diff: the render target relocation guard works

fritchii-reloc-guard-addr on fritchii-relocate-v2.diff: the render target relocation guard works
by address too (garbled dialogue text). Apply after fritchii-relocate-v2.diff (it does not apply
on T82 alone or on fritchii-relocate.diff v1; for v1 use fritchii-reloc-guard-addr.diff). Same
change as that diff; only the 600-frame "Render target relocation" hunk is rebased onto v2's
line (which gained the exact-frame-boundary count). No new switch: it only acts inside
EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_RELOCATE=1's relocation, which it makes refuse more.

Upstream: Frizti/Fritchii b3396c01f9 "texture_cache: relocation guard by address too (garbled
dialogue text)" (Frizti, with Claude Opus 5.5), released in fritchii-v5.1 (2026-11-09), unchanged
in fritchii-v5.2. It fixes Fritchii's EXP43 relocation (07b38b3caf, 86a04911af), which
fritchii-relocate-v2.diff ports.

What it fixes (Fritchii v5.1 notes and commit): OoT draws each dialogue box's text into a render
target at one address, sized to the box. The guard was per shape (format and size), so every new
box size was relocated once before its own guard tripped, and that box's text showed scraps of
other images (the owner's v5 session: dozens of guard trips at 0x8113100000, one per box size).
A guard trip now also protects its address.

Changes (as upstream):
- NoteRelocationGuard: every trip ORs its reason into relocation_guarded_addresses[image.gpu_addr]
  (before the shape's early return, so later trips on an already guarded shape note their address
  too). Only with EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_RELOCATE=1 (review fix: with EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_COLD alone the map
  only grew, one entry per tripped address for the session, and nothing read it).
- JoinImages: a candidate is kept (counted in relocation_guarded) when its shape is guarded OR the
  target's new address or the old image's address is in relocation_guarded_addresses.
- texture_cache_base.h: the map (Common::unordered_map<GPUVAddr, u8>, sticky for the session like
  relocation_shapes; one entry per guarded image address).
Deviation: a counter of candidates kept by the address alone (relocation_guarded_by_address) and
the map's size are added to the 600-frame "Render target relocation" line, so a run shows whether
the address guard ever fires ("({} by the address alone)", "{} addresses guarded"). Upstream only
counts them in relocation_guarded. The cold sweep (EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_COLD) still reads the shape
guard only, as upstream.

Unset EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_RELOCATE and EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_COLD: nothing runs (NoteRelocationGuard and
the relocation block are behind FritchiiRelocationGuards()/FritchiiRelocate()), byte-identical
behaviour. With only COLD set: one cached bool test per trip, nothing stored, as before.
Memory: the map is sticky and unbounded like relocation_shapes, but keyed by address, so a
drifting chain whose members trip adds one entry per address (16 bytes plus table overhead);
the log line's "{} addresses guarded" shows the growth.

diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
index 71b90ac..c3c9cfd 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
@@ -1286,17 +1286,19 @@ void TextureCache<P>::TickRelocation() {
     }
     LOG_INFO(HW_GPU,
              "Render target relocation (EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_RELOCATE={}) last 600 frames: {} "
-             "candidates, {} kept by the guard, {} relocated, {} over 2+ images of their shape; {} "
-             "of {} shapes guarded; {} cleared targets over bad overlaps waited for an exact frame "
-             "boundary{}",
+             "candidates, {} kept by the guard ({} by the address alone), {} relocated, {} over 2+ "
+             "images of their shape; {} of {} shapes guarded, {} addresses guarded; {} cleared "
+             "targets over bad overlaps waited for an exact frame boundary{}",
              FritchiiRelocate() ? 1 : 0, relocation_candidates, relocation_guarded,
-             relocation_relocated, relocation_crowded, guarded_shapes, relocation_shapes.size(),
+             relocation_guarded_by_address, relocation_relocated, relocation_crowded,
+             guarded_shapes, relocation_shapes.size(), relocation_guarded_addresses.size(),
              relocation_unreliable,
              Tegra::g_nx2_render_clock_lost.load(std::memory_order_relaxed)
                  ? " (clock lost: relocation off for the session)"
                  : "");
     relocation_candidates = relocation_guarded = relocation_relocated = relocation_crowded = 0;
     relocation_unreliable = 0;
+    relocation_guarded_by_address = 0;
 }
 
 template <class P>
@@ -4798,8 +4800,13 @@ ImageId TextureCache<P>::JoinImages(const ImageInfo& info, GPUVAddr gpu_addr, DA
             RelocationShape& shape = relocation_shapes[RelocationShapeKey(new_info)];
             relocation_seen = true;
             ++relocation_candidates;
-            if (shape.guard != 0) {
+            // The guard by address too (Fritchii b3396c01f9): a trip also protects the address of
+            // the image it tripped on, checked for the target's new and old address.
+            const bool address_guarded = relocation_guarded_addresses.contains(gpu_addr) ||
+                                         relocation_guarded_addresses.contains(old_gpu_addr);
+            if (shape.guard != 0 || address_guarded) {
                 ++relocation_guarded;
+                relocation_guarded_by_address += shape.guard == 0 ? 1 : 0;
             } else {
                 if (!shape.relocated_logged) {
                     shape.relocated_logged = true;
@@ -6068,6 +6075,11 @@ ImageId TextureCache<P>::RelocationCandidate(const ImageInfo& new_info, GPUVAddr
 template <class P>
 void TextureCache<P>::NoteRelocationGuard(ImageBase& image, RelocationGuard reason) {
     image.relocation_guard_noted |= reason;
+    // Every trip notes its address (Fritchii b3396c01f9), also when the shape was guarded already.
+    // Only the relocation reads it, so with EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_COLD alone nothing is kept.
+    if (FritchiiRelocate()) {
+        relocation_guarded_addresses[image.gpu_addr] |= reason;
+    }
     RelocationShape& shape = relocation_shapes[RelocationShapeKey(image.info)];
     if ((shape.guard & reason) != 0) {
         return;
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
index d111d39..e436c90 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
@@ -668,9 +668,16 @@ private:
         u32 same_frame_refused{}; ///< Since the last report (render-frame clock line)
     };
     ::Common::unordered_map<u64, RelocationShape> relocation_shapes;
+    /// The guard by address too (Fritchii b3396c01f9, fritchii-v5.1): each trip also guards the
+    /// address of the image it tripped on (its RelocationGuard bits), and JoinImages checks a
+    /// target's new and old address. OoT draws each dialogue box's text into a render target at
+    /// one address, sized to the box: per shape, every new box size was relocated once before its
+    /// own guard tripped, and that box's text showed other images' contents. Sticky, as the shapes.
+    ::Common::unordered_map<GPUVAddr, u8> relocation_guarded_addresses;
     /// Since the last report (TickRelocation, every 600 frames once a candidate was seen).
     u64 relocation_candidates{};
     u64 relocation_guarded{};
+    u64 relocation_guarded_by_address{}; ///< Of relocation_guarded: the shape was not guarded
     u64 relocation_relocated{};
     u64 relocation_crowded{}; ///< Cleared targets over two or more images of their shape
     u64 relocation_same_frame{}; ///< Candidates whose only predecessors were written this frame
